# R5 (task 165): pin the CI workflow to LF in the worktree.
#
# Why: tools/validate_workflow.js asserts the workflow contains no CR, because a
# stray \r in a `run:` block breaks the shell step it lands in. This host has
# core.autocrlf=true, so without this rule a fresh Windows clone checks the file
# out as CRLF and the fast gate fails for a reason that has nothing to do with
# the workflow being wrong — the machine-dependent class of bug task 164 just
# removed from the offline manifest (see tools/manifest_hash.js).
#
# Scope: workflows only. game/ and docs/ are intentionally NOT pinned — they stay
# CRLF-tolerant and are compared through the canonical-bytes helper instead.
.github/workflows/*.yml text eol=lf
.github/workflows/*.yaml text eol=lf
